    "summary": "Root cause of the L2-1 failure: an instance-layer defect on support line 1 (Pier 1). The Pier 1 bearing is a plain laminated elastomeric bearing 600×700 mm with seven 11 mm internal rubber layers, but the KG's bearing formulas could not read its t1_mm from the instance and fell back to a default 8 mm layer (te=0.056 instead of 0.077). Consequently the code-clause recomputations during the L2-1 check (shape factor S, vertical stiffness Kv, shear stiffness Kh from JTG 3362-2018 8.7) disagreed with the accepted decisions (S=20.19 vs 14.69; Kv=15.72e6 vs 8.03e6; Kh=15000 vs 10909). Re-writing support 1's bearing instance (t1_mm=11, n_layers=7) restored the correct inputs, and all recomputations now match the accepted decisions. No decisions needed revising.\n\nModel: 3-span cast-in-place continuous box girder (35+45+35 m), spine-beam 2D idealization on piers; single-cell cast_box section (A=6.712 m^2, I=4.498 m^4), C50 with measured Ec=37000 MPa; self-weight only w=174.512 kN/m (m=17.789 t/m); twin 1.8 m C40 pier columns (Pier 1 h=20 m, Pier 2 h=27 m); laminated elastomeric bearings (Pier 1 fixed, others PTFE sliding); Highway Class I, one-way, 3 lanes, xi=0.78, qk=10.5 kN/m, Pk=330/350/330 kN, mu=0.181 (f1=3.037 Hz).\n\nResults: f1=3.037 Hz; self-weight reactions 2241/7780/7779/2249 kN; max lane positive moment +11474 kN·m (mid-span 2), max negative -9093 kN·m. Model passed L1/L2/L3 checks."
